    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! \u2705 The bug is fixed. Here's what was wrong and how I fixed it:\n\n## Problem\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't creating `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`, even though running `frai-gate init --ci` directly worked. Only `FRAI-SPEC.md` was being created.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe root program defines `--ci` as a global option (line 605). When you run `frai gate init --ci`, commander consumes the `--ci` flag at the program level, so the gate subcommand only receives `['init']` instead of `['init', '--ci']`.\n\n## Solution\nModified the `gate` command's action handler to capture raw arguments from `process.argv` instead of relying on commander's parsed args:\n\n```typescript\n// Use raw process.argv to preserve all flags (e.g. --ci) that commander may consume at program level\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex !== -1 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : args ?? [];\n```\n\nThis ensures all arguments after \"gate\" (including flags) are preserved and forwarded to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n## Changes Made\n- **Modified:** `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 737-756)\n- **Rebuilt:** `packages/frai-cli` with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- **Verified:** `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both files",
